{
  "dom_id": "step-q117179",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195146/assets/e0a9d0aeba77f3ca2cd472b9c65df156394990a89a643e9a316ee662a52eb6b3.png)\n\nDavid wants to redesign his house, changing a small window for a big square window. The dimensions of the square window are shown in the figure above. What area covers the window?",
  "worked_solution": "The area of a square with sides of length $a$ is given by \n\n$$\nA={a}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that $a=4\\,m.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={a}^{2}={4}^{2}=16\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
